  "caption": "Quinn's first ski trip: very confident, then the knees went in and Quinn went down. Now the inner knee is very unhappy.\n\nThe MCL runs along the inside of the knee and stops it caving inwards. It can be strained by a blow to the outer knee or a twisting fall. Most MCL sprains heal well with rehab; mild ones may settle in weeks, bigger ones take longer.\n\nWhat often helps: keep moving and weight-bearing as tolerated, restore range first, protect the knee from inward pushes, strengthen the hips and thighs with squats, step-ups and band side walks, and return to sport in stages.\n\nRapid swelling, a deep pop, locking or the knee giving way are worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
